;; kontor-substrate — the dependency-light value layer of the kontor kernel.
;;
;; This is the FIRST kontor module carved out with its own deps.edn, because
;; it is the first with an EXTERNAL consumer: the dvergr agent harness depends
;; on `kontor.money` to represent LLM/compute costs as commodity-tagged
;; BigDecimals (its metering subledger) WITHOUT pulling the full accounting
;; kernel (datahike, instaparse, mustang, …). See kontor research note 190.
;;
;; Contents today: `kontor.money` (Money record + commodity-checked arithmetic
;; + HALF_EVEN rounding, ADR-013). It has ZERO datahike dependency — the
;; `{:db/id N}` handling in `posting->money` is pure map-shape matching. As more
;; genuinely dep-light primitives prove reusable (commodity/dimension
;; vocabulary), they land here.
;;
;; The kontor monorepo root deps.edn also merges `modules/substrate/src` onto
;; its shared classpath, so the kernel keeps seeing `kontor.money` unchanged —
;; this file only makes the module independently consumable via :local/root
;; (or, later, a published `org.replikativ/kontor-substrate` coordinate).
{:paths ["src"]
 :deps  {org.clojure/clojure {:mvn/version "1.12.4"}}

 :aliases
 {:test
  {:extra-paths ["test"]
   :extra-deps  {lambdaisland/kaocha    {:mvn/version "1.91.1392"}
                 org.clojure/test.check {:mvn/version "1.1.1"}}
   :main-opts   ["-m" "kaocha.runner"]}}}
